      "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
      "instance_name": "Anti_Latino_Hispanic_stereotypes",
      "label": "Anti-Latino/Hispanic stereotypes",
      "description": "Stereotypes that portray Latinos or Hispanics in a negative or derogatory way, such as associating them with criminality, laziness, or being 'anchor babies.' The meme, by misrepresenting Cinco de Mayo and associating it with Puerto Rico, can be seen as reinforcing or mocking these stereotypes by implying that Latinos or Hispanics are only associated with American or Puerto Rican culture, which can be seen as disrespectful or insensitive to those who celebrate Cinco de Mayo or Puerto Rican culture.",
