    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5ca424e1",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
      "label": "The text 'happy cinco de ported!' is mapped onto the man holding American flags, implying he represents a Puerto Rican person celebrating a fictional holiday.",
      "description": "The text 'happy cinco de ported!' is a deliberate misspelling intended to imply 'Cinco de Puerto Rico'. This text is juxtaposed with the visual of a man holding American flags, which are associated with the United States. The mapping suggests that the man, through his visual representation (holding American flags), is being analogically mapped as a representative of Puerto Rico (a U.S. territory) celebrating this fictional holiday. This creates a false association and is part of the meme's cultural mockery and appropriation.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
